  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNDP, 2018-2022, GDPP Governance Program i Ethiopien</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP, 2018-2022,GDPP Governance Programme Ethiopia - UNDP, 2018-2022, Governance Programme Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till demokratiska institutioner som lyder under parlamentet i syfte att st&#xe4;rka dess m&#xf6;jligheter att genomf&#xf6;ra sitt mandat p&#xe5; ett mer oberoende s&#xe4;tt.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the main accountability mechanism in Ethiopia in order to contribute to that they can implement their core mandate in a more independent and professional manner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the programme, that is managed by the UNDP and implemented by Ethiopian state institutions, including the Ethiopian Human Rights Commission, NEBE, the Ombudsman, The Federal Court, the Anti-Corruption Commission, Ministry of Peace, and the Parliament, to strengthen key democratic functions, are as follows:

1. Political processes of federal and regional state legislative bodies are more inclusive and effectively delivering on their constitutional mandates. 
2. Federal and regional state systems of governance are more accountable, transparent and are delivering public services in a more inclusive and responsive ways.
3. Citizens are more empowered to voice their concern and actively participate in decision making processes at all levels of the governance and political systems. 
4. Systems and mechanisms for promoting social cohesion, managing diversity, preventing and managing conflicts, fostering dialogues and building peace are further strengthened at national, regional and local levels.
5. Access to justice enhanced and human rights promoted and protected across Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
